    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Tunable knobs for <xref href=\"Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkerProcessingRetryPipeline\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>:\nthe Polly-based retry wrapping <code>worker.ProcessAsync</code> in\n<code>WorkManager.ProcessCloudEventAsync</code>.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">Deliberately separate from <xref href=\"Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.DaprResilienceOptions\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> even\nthough the defaults happen to match: that class scopes Dapr <em sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"6\">infra</em>\ncall retries (state store, pubsub RPCs), this one scopes worker\n<em sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerProcessingRetryOptions.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"8\">business-logic</em> processing failures -- restoring the\npubsub-topics spec's &quot;Retry Policy on Dapr Subscribe Exceptions&quot;\nbounded-retry-then-dead-letter guarantee, which the streaming\nPubsub.Subscribe migration moved from Dapr's broker-level redelivery\nto WorkManager's own application-level responsibility (broker\nredelivery is architecturally inapplicable once a message is inside\nthe Gateway's multi-consumer fan-out -- see spec's &quot;In-process\nexception on a subscriber&quot; requirement).</p>\n"
    },
    {
