      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Hosted service that automatically recovers workers on application startup,\ngated by <xref href=\"Virtufin.WorkManager.Configuration.WorkerRecoveryOptions.Enabled\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and coordinated across\nmultiple WorkManager instances via <xref href=\"Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.RecoveryLeaderElector\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">When multiple instances start concurrently, only the leader performs\nrecovery — the others wait for the leader lease to expire (or be released)\nbefore they would attempt to take over. This avoids the N×W engine-load\nwaste described in WM #4.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"10\">Kestrel readiness is gated via <xref href=\"Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.RecoveryHealthCheck\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>:</p>\n<ul sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\">\n<li sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\"><code>Degraded</code> while recovery is in progress.</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\"><code>Unhealthy</code> if recovery failed.</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/Virtufin.WorkManager.Services.WorkManagerRecoveryHostedService.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"13\"><code>Healthy</code> once recovery completes (whether this instance performed it\nor another leader did).</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
